NAME
       unlink - remove one file name

SYNOPSIS
       unlink FILE

DESCRIPTION
       unlink removes exactly one file name (a link) with no options and no
       questions, like a bare rm FILE. The file's data is freed when its last
       hard link is gone and no program has it open. unlink does not remove
       directories.

EXAMPLES
           unlink /tmp/oldlink

SEE ALSO
       rm(1), ln(1)
